{"tuid":"1h64lfvpn9rd54bn","pageVersion":6,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-26T10:05:51.224Z","record":{"colophon":{"generator":"ifdb.org/viewgame","generatorversion":1,"originated":"2026-10-25"},"identification":{"ifids":["C2B23038-8274-41F6-A743-7E2D2D0CF02D"],"format":"glulx"},"bibliographic":{"title":"The Count and the Communist","author":"Tristan Pun","language":"en","firstpublished":"2026-09-01","genre":"Adventure, Espionage, Dialectical materialism","description":"<i>My dear, the Revolution is in danger</i> <br> <br>The year is 1918, and the Great War ended a few days earlier. However, in a remote mansion somewhere in France, enemies of the people actively seek to pursue the conflict on a new front. As a Communist, you must uncover the sinister schemes being hatched; but, as a laundress recently hired at this mansion, you also have the responsibility of doing the laundry and getting on with the household staff. <br> <br>The game offers an immersive adventure, full of twists and turns, grounded in real historical events. As you explore, infiltrate and talk to people, you will discover a world not so different from our own, one confronted with both incredible new technologies and the everyday violence of class-based society. <br> <br>You will also discover, in a somewhat unconventional use of Inform 7, a fully-fledged ASCII-style graphical interface, playable exclusively via the keyboard, the source code for which is included in the downloadable archive. Note that the game *cannot* be played on a mobile device. <br> <br>No rest until all peoples are liberated!"},"contacts":[],"ifdb":{"tuid":"1h64lfvpn9rd54bn","pageversion":6,"link":"https://ifdb.org/viewgame?id=1h64lfvpn9rd54bn","coverart":{"url":"https://ifdb.org/coverart?id=1h64lfvpn9rd54bn&version=6"},"playTimeInMinutes":360,"primaryPlayOnlineUrl":"https://debeauharnais.itch.io/the-count-and-the-communist","downloads":{"links":[{"url":"https://debeauharnais.itch.io/the-count-and-the-communist","playOnlineUrl":"https://d